Subject: register VM: publish each frame's register window as a GC root range

What this does:
  Every register-VM frame now records where its live registers are and how many
  there are (`JSStackFrame.rv_regs` / `rv_nregs`), and a single walker,
  `regvm_for_each_root_range`, visits them along the `prev_frame` chain. This
  is stage D1 of the deferred-RC plan
  (`HP-S3-DEFERRED-RC-PLAN-2026-10-02.md` section 3): it is the registry the
  ZCT reconcile pass and the later register-ownership flip will both scan, and
  it changes no ownership yet.

  The window excludes the last handshake slot, which holds the control-stack
  depth as an integer rather than a value: `rv_nregs` is
  `regvm_reg_count + REGVM_HS - 1`. The four places that build a register frame
  -- `regvm_record_fill`, the in-loop call macro, the fresh `JS_CallInternal`
  bytecode path, and `async_func_init` -- set it; the three C-frame helpers
  (`js_call_c_function_data`, `js_call_c_closure`, `js_call_c_function`) set it
  to NULL/0 so a native frame is never mistaken for a register root.

  `QJS_DRC_VALIDATE` adds a debug validator, run from `JS_RunGC`, that asserts
  every counted value in a root range is still owned (count >= 1). It holds
  while registers own, and is the check that catches a missed `js_dup` in the
  D4 ownership flip. Both switches default to off; `QJS_DRC` is the umbrella
  that stage D2 turns on.

  In a build that does not turn on the deferred-RC collector the two stores are
  compiled out (`REGVM_SET_ROOT` is a no-op), so D1 is instruction-neutral there;
  it costs nothing until `QJS_DRC` is enabled in stage D2.

